      "id": 112068,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-08-04T12:52:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think about the only time you  don't  get to apply a buff twice in the same power is with Mr Fixer's Dual Crowbars, where it specifies that the second hit has to be the same damage as the first, so it doesn't get buffed again.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, crowbar's intent is to just turn his basic Strike of \"1 target 1 damage\" into \"2 targets 1 damage\". Sacrosanct and Isothermic take in one instance of damage and output a second, so its slightly different.<br>&nbsp;</p>",
